    {
     "page": 1,
     "text": "Ford Mcdonald and Clinic\n\nDear Colleague,\n\nI saw Jeremy Blackburn, a 71-year-old male, in consultation on August 22, 2025. Mr. Blackburn presented with benign prostatic hyperplasia (BPH) which has been well controlled. His current medications include finasteride 1 mg daily.\n\nUpon evaluation, Mr. Blackburn’s blood pressure was recorded at 123/86 mmHg and his weight was 164 pounds. His physical exam was unremarkable aside from expected findings related to his age and BPH. There were no signs of urinary retention or infection.\n\nMr. Blackburn reports adherence to his prescribed regimen and experiences no adverse effects. His lifestyle includes moderate alcohol consumption at approximately 12 drinks per week, but he denies any tobacco use. His family history is pertinent for his mother, who had a myocardial infarction at age 55 and passed away at 54, and another myocardial infarction at age 80, passing away at 91.\n\nMy impression is that Mr. Blackburn’s BPH is well-managed with finasteride. I recommend continuing his current treatment plan and regular monitoring.\n\nThank you for this referral. Please feel free to contact me if further information or management adjustments are needed.\n\nSincerely,\n\nDr. Davis \nFamily Medicine \nFord Mcdonald and Matthews Clinic\n"
    }
